> Gleki, you said "Anyway, I can't see any language that would distinguish
> them probably because human eye sees every star in the sky except the Sun
> with protrusions i.e. as a "star polygon"."
>
> I disagree. I would say that people see NO star (or planet) as having
> protrusions. They're just bright points. Camera/photographic artifacts do
> add points sometimes.
>

No, human eye does see them with protrusions. Camera obviously doesn't.
Human eye sees them that way. That's how it is constructed.


